# The contract each file in this repository is held to, read by `check-conformance.sh` beside it.
#
# Vendored from Jerome-Group/.github and adapted for a standalone repository (ADR-0002): where
# the Organisation generated this file and served it from outside the checked tree, here it is
# maintained by hand and lives inside the tree it binds. That is a deliberate trade — this
# repository can edit its own contract, and the pull request that edits a bound file edits its
# manifest record in the same diff.
#
# Record classes, tab-separated:
#   originals  <name>            the seed the `required` origins refer to; never this repository
#   required   <path>  <origin>  the file must exist; the origin says where its text came from
#   skeleton   <path>  <ceiling> the file's headings are checked, and its length when not `-`
#   heading    <path>  <text>    one required heading, in the order the records appear
#   seed-only  <path>            carried by the seed, checked by nothing — a gift, not a contract
#
# There are no `mirrored` records: the org pinned mirrored files to a hash because its seed
# silently overwrites edits, and no seed reaches this repository. Edited documents are simply
# `required` (ADR-0002).
